 "segments": [
  "[  0.00-  2.20] He bent the rollercoaster's loop out of shape.",
  "[  2.44-  6.62] You see, it's the first ride ever to go upside down, and it cost him everything.",
  "[  6.90-  9.42] So of course his rival copies it bolt for bolt.",
  "[  9.60- 13.68] But the night before opening, his test dummy comes back crushed like a soda can,",
  "[ 13.84- 17.96] but he can't miss the opening, so he grabs a hammer and beats the bottom into a long,",
  "[ 18.12- 18.88] lazy curve.",
  "[ 19.12- 19.98] Does he know what he's doing?",
  "[ 20.24- 20.78] Not really.",
  "[ 20.98- 25.42] His rival laughs, then sneaks in and cranks the sides together until the loop is tall",
  "[ 25.42- 28.18] and skinny, so the first cart will snap like a twig.",
  "[ 28.18- 31.58] The next morning, the town lines up at the rival's perfect circle,",
  "[ 31.82- 33.62] and the rival climbs in front to show off.",
  "[ 33.84- 37.00] The owner climbs into his, and as his cart tips over the first hill,",
  "[ 37.14- 39.64] he finally sees the tall, skinny loop ahead.",
  "[ 39.80- 40.86] But it's too late.",
  "[ 41.08- 43.74] You see, a car can creep around a hairpin turn at five,",
  "[ 43.94- 45.58] but take it at 60 and it flips.",
  "[ 45.92- 48.08] A cart is fastest at the bottom of a loop,",
  "[ 48.20- 50.48] and a perfect circle puts a hairpin right there,",
  "[ 50.66- 51.86] which is what crushed the dummy.",
  "[ 52.04- 53.72] But his hammer made the bottom gentle,",
  "[ 53.90- 56.24] and the rival's squeeze moved the hairpin up top,",
  "[ 56.24- 57.48] where the cart is crawling,",
  "[ 57.74- 59.46] so he floats over without a scratch,",
  "[ 59.74- 62.86] just as the rival's cart hits the bottom of that perfect circle."
 ],
